 the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 15284, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_018yRhPC4BwkwjUgTqikc5aq", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15284, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018yRhPC4BwkwjUgTqikc5aq", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18660, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened incident INC-0001 as a SEV2, which paged on-call.\n\n- **The problem:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with about 18% of requests erroring.\n- **Which version I rolled back to:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. A later build, v2.3.1-rc, was only ever healthy in staging, so I didn't use it.\n- **Result:** All three regions are now on v2.3.0, the error rate is about 0.2%, and the service reports healthy.\n- **Incident:** It describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's redeployed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VVKBjGAFj4TC95wm5EpQ48", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FpU8eQ9dCatxh6PfjvdUYQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Most recent production-healthy release is v2.3.0 (v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging). Rolling back.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014sMuoSGBEkAmUAJMKCqGem", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JMZkL5K9j67vPLpUNP2Bko", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016xEXviPsKaMnr5LkHPLGCE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018yRhPC4BwkwjUgTqikc5aq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging.) After the rollback, the service reports healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened incident INC-0001 as a SEV2, which paged on-call.\n\n- **The problem:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with about 18% of requests erroring.\n- **Which version I rolled back to:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. A later build, v2.3.1-rc, was only ever healthy in staging, so I didn't use it.\n- **Result:** All three regions are now on v2.3.0, the error rate is about 0.2%, and the service reports healthy.\n- **Incident:** It describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's redeployed.", "type": "text"}]}]}